---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const updated = new Date(SITE.legalUpdated).toLocaleDateString('en-CA', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---

<Page
  title="Terms of Use | WorldTripMap"
  description="The terms for using WorldTripMap: what you can do with the posters you make, what the maps are and are not suitable for, and the limits of our responsibility."
  h1="Terms of use"
  lede="Plain terms for a simple tool. By using WorldTripMap you agree to them."
  crumb="Terms"
  path="/terms/"
>
  <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}.</p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <p>
    WorldTripMap is free to use and does not require an account. You may use it for yourself, your family, your classroom or your
    business. Please do not try to disrupt the site, overload it with automated requests, or use it to break the law.
  </p>

  <h2>What you make is yours</h2>
  <p>
    The maps and posters you create show your own travels and your own words, and you are free to download, print, share and display
    them. You are responsible for the text you add: do not use a poster to mislead, harass or impersonate anyone.
  </p>
  <p>
    The WorldTripMap name, logo, website design and code remain ours. Turning off the small site mark on a poster is allowed. Presenting
    the tool itself as your own product is not.
  </p>

  <h2>What the maps are for</h2>
  <p>
    The maps are simplified drawings made for marking and displaying places you have been. They are not suitable for navigation, for
    surveying, or as evidence of where a legal boundary lies. Boundaries and names follow the sources described on the{' '}
    <a href="/methodology/">data and methods page</a> and do not express a position on any territorial dispute.
  </p>
  <p>
    We work to keep facts on the site accurate and to correct mistakes when they are reported, but we cannot promise that everything is
    complete or current. Check anything important against an official source.
  </p>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>
    Your maps are stored in your own browser and can be lost if you clear your browser’s data, switch devices, or use a private window.
    Keep a share link or a downloaded poster if a map matters to you. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> explains this in full.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty, and limits on liability</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided as it is, without warranties of any kind. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for losses that
    result from using it, including a lost map, a print that did not turn out as expected, or a decision made using information found
    here.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party material</h2>
  <p>
    Map data comes from Natural Earth and is in the public domain. The typefaces are used under the SIL Open Font License. Links to
    other websites are provided for reference, and we are not responsible for their content.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update the site and these terms. When the terms change in a way that matters, the date at the top will change. If you keep
    using the site after a change, the new terms apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
